    refEn: 'Ockham\'s Razor',
    fullSourceEn: 'Principle of parsimony of William of Ockham, formulated in several works, such as the Commentary on the Sentences (I, d. 30, q. 1) and the Summa Logicae (c. 1323). The best-known formula, "entia non sunt multiplicanda praeter necessitatem", does not appear in his texts: it is from the Franciscan John Punch (1639).',
